{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Remember these.</b> That you did while you were in my land." "And the meaning of <b>for you are my servant</b>: after you were already my servant, acknowledge your former transgressions, for I desire that you be a servant to me." "And the meaning of <b>[a servant to me]</b>: you alone." "<b>You bore me.</b> From the nif'al binyan, and in my opinion it is so: do not bear me away from me — remember me, and I will remember you."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {3 "The lemma תנשני is read as from נשה 'to forget/bear away'; Ibn Ezra reads לא תנשה as the Aramaic-influenced form written in Hebrew characters, resolving the abbreviated final letter."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:02.118924685Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}